# Scoped to ui/ deliberately (story c2-1, AC 10).
#
# The repository has core.autocrlf=true and no root .gitattributes, so without this file
# ui/ checks out CRLF on Windows and LF on ubuntu CI. Prettier's `endOfLine: "lf"` treats
# CRLF as a formatting violation, which makes `prettier --check` red for the project lead
# and green in CI from the same commit — worse than no gate at all.
#
# A root-level .gitattributes would renormalise every tracked file in the repository, which
# is not this story's change. Setting prettier's `endOfLine: "auto"` was the alternative and
# was rejected: it lets CRLF and LF both pass, and c2-2/c2-3's `git diff --exit-code` drift
# checks need one deterministic byte sequence.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must not be normalised. `* text=auto eol=lf` above would otherwise line-ending-
# normalise them on checkout under core.autocrlf=true — silently, on Windows only, on a fresh
# clone — and a font that has been through that does not decode.
#
# The FONT FAMILY, not just the one member that ships today (story c2-5). Only .woff2 is
# committed; .woff, .ttf and .otf are listed because the cost of listing them is nothing and the
# cost of a later story adding a fallback subset without remembering this line is a corruption
# that CI cannot see — CI is ubuntu, where core.autocrlf is off. spa.py already registers a
# media type for .woff for the same reason.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
